<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<usx version="3.0">
  <book code="2JN" style="id"/>
  <para style="h">2 John</para>
  <para style="toc2">2 John</para>
  <para style="toc1">Second John</para>
  <para style="mt1">Second John</para>
  <chapter number="1" style="c" sid="2JN 1"/>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="1" style="v" sid="2JN 1:1"/>This letter comes from the elder<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:1. </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Understood to be John.</char></note> to the chosen lady<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:1. </char><char style="ft" closed="false">The “chosen lady” could refer to a church, or to a specific Christian lady. Similarly in verse 13.</char></note> and her children, whom I love in the truth. Not just from me, but from everyone who knows the truth, <verse eid="2JN 1:1"/><verse number="2" style="v" sid="2JN 1:2"/>because the truth lives in us and will be with us forever. <verse eid="2JN 1:2"/><verse number="3" style="v" sid="2JN 1:3"/>May grace, mercy and peace continue to be with us, from God the Father and from Jesus Christ, the Son of the Father, in truth and in love.<verse eid="2JN 1:3"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="4" style="v" sid="2JN 1:4"/>I was delighted to discover that some of your children are following the truth, just as the Father commanded us. <verse eid="2JN 1:4"/><verse number="5" style="v" sid="2JN 1:5"/>Now I'm telling you, dear lady, not as a new instruction, but following what we've understood from the beginning, that we should love one another. <verse eid="2JN 1:5"/><verse number="6" style="v" sid="2JN 1:6"/>This is what love is: we should follow God's commands. The command, just as you heard right from the beginning, is that you should live in love.<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:6. </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Or “that you should behave this way.”</char></note><verse eid="2JN 1:6"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="7" style="v" sid="2JN 1:7"/>I'm telling you this because many deceivers have left and gone out into the world. They don't accept that Jesus Christ has come as a human being. Anyone like this is a deceiver and an antichrist. <verse eid="2JN 1:7"/><verse number="8" style="v" sid="2JN 1:8"/>Be careful that you don't lose what we've worked so hard for, and that you receive all that you should.<verse eid="2JN 1:8"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="9" style="v" sid="2JN 1:9"/>All those who become extremists<note caller="+" style="f"><char style="fr" closed="false">1:9. </char><char style="ft" closed="false">Literally, “who go too far.”</char></note> and don't continue to follow the teaching of Christ don't have God with them. Those who continue to follow the teaching of Christ have both the Father and the Son with them. <verse eid="2JN 1:9"/><verse number="10" style="v" sid="2JN 1:10"/>If people come to you and don't show evidence of Christ's teaching, don't take them in, don't welcome them— <verse eid="2JN 1:10"/><verse number="11" style="v" sid="2JN 1:11"/>for if you encourage them you share in their evil work.<verse eid="2JN 1:11"/></para>
  <para style="p">
    <verse number="12" style="v" sid="2JN 1:12"/>I have so many things to tell you that I won't write any more with paper and ink, for I hope to visit you and talk with you face to face. How happy that would make us! <verse eid="2JN 1:12"/><verse number="13" style="v" sid="2JN 1:13"/>Greetings to you from the children of your chosen sister.<verse eid="2JN 1:13"/></para>
  <para style="b"/>
  <chapter eid="2JN 1"/>
</usx>
